  "description": "<div>\n<p>Rotate an n-by-n matrix 90 degrees clockwise in place without allocating another n-by-n matrix. Return the modified matrix after the rotation so the grader can compare its value; mutating it and returning nothing does not satisfy this task.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = [[1,2],[3,4]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[3,1],[4,2]]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The left column becomes the top row.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = [[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[7,4,1],[8,5,2],[9,6,3]]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The outer ring moves clockwise; 5 stays put.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> matrix = [[42]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[42]]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> A single cell cannot move.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 10</code>.</li>\n<li>The matrix has exactly n rows and n columns.</li>\n<li>Each entry is an integer in <code>[-1000, 1000]</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
